    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8932dd9_cde95a0c",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-05T05:19:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To make a socket connection to a process running in the VM.",
      "parentUuid": "2cb1eb76_a0ccd566",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 232,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "17774711ec57abbf06bb7f2be8254db758fad505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6b8adcd_cde31024",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-05T05:42:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried that \"integer\" can be a dangling pointer or even point to an unrelated VM instance. For now I\u0027m fine, but we might need a safer way to get \"address of VM instance created by the app\".",
      "parentUuid": "c8932dd9_cde95a0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 232,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "17774711ec57abbf06bb7f2be8254db758fad505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60a0e029_b614e5be",
        "filename": "javalib/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 232,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-05T05:53:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CID by itself doesn\u0027t provide any protection. Anyone can use any CID. It\u0027s the job of the program waiting for a connection on the CID/port to protect itself from unauthorized clients.",
      "parentUuid": "e6b8adcd_cde31024",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 232,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 232,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "17774711ec57abbf06bb7f2be8254db758fad505",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
